-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_newlines_err_cr_string.pcpp - Lexical: a string a lone CR ends

  Break step of lex_newlines: a lone CR is a newline, and a string ends
  at its line's end at the latest, so a string a lone CR cuts off is
  unterminated, LX0001, where it starts; the line after the CR is read
  on its own.
  Its bytes are part of the test (see above): edit it with an editor
  that keeps them as they are.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_newlines_err_cr_string;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
  @@end
*/

begin
  println("ab // ERROR LX0001@11  );
end.
